WEBVTT

00:04.662 --> 00:07.750
Welcome to Clover Bottom Quarry, in Jackson County,

00:07.750 --> 00:11.812
Kentucky, near McKee, along US 421.

00:11.812 --> 00:14.263
It's owned and operated by The Allen Company.

00:14.263 --> 00:16.900
This drawing is only an illustration to help you

00:16.900 --> 00:19.463
picture how the pieces fit. Your instructor will

00:19.463 --> 00:20.975
show you the real map.

00:22.105 --> 00:24.204
The most important thing to understand about Clover

00:24.204 --> 00:27.042
Bottom is that there are two separate MSHA mines

00:27.042 --> 00:30.267
here, sharing one surface. The old mine,

00:30.267 --> 00:35.442
number one, has mine ID 15-00112. It was operated

00:35.442 --> 00:38.267
by M.A. Walker beginning around 1950,

00:38.267 --> 00:41.517
and Allen bought it in 2004. The new mine,

00:41.517 --> 00:47.304
number two, has mine ID 15-19898. Allen opened

00:47.304 --> 00:48.767
it in 2021.

00:49.878 --> 00:52.941
Each mine has its own escapeways, its own maps

00:52.941 --> 00:55.965
and its own check-in record. So every shift,

00:55.965 --> 00:58.128
confirm which mine you're assigned to,

00:58.128 --> 01:01.478
old or new. Procedures differ by mine even though

01:01.478 --> 01:03.178
the surface is shared.

01:04.308 --> 01:06.896
Both are one-level underground limestone mines

01:06.896 --> 01:11.296
using room and pillar, with rooms about 30 by 40 feet.

01:11.296 --> 01:13.708
In the old mine, the floor is mined.

01:13.708 --> 01:16.096
In the new mine, headers are mined.

01:16.096 --> 01:18.746
Floor mining and header mining have different face

01:18.746 --> 01:21.146
conditions, so what you learn about the face in

01:21.146 --> 01:23.696
one mine doesn't automatically carry over to the

01:23.696 --> 01:24.421
other.

01:25.554 --> 01:28.816
Clover Bottom also drills and blasts on the surface,

01:28.816 --> 01:32.241
with benches about 65 feet high. Allen's own crew

01:32.241 --> 01:34.779
does the drilling and blasting, and sometimes a

01:34.779 --> 01:38.466
contractor, Austin Powder, works on the surface.

01:38.466 --> 01:41.241
Shot rock is hauled to the pit, where the primary

01:41.241 --> 01:44.216
crusher is, then conveyed up the hill to the secondary

01:44.216 --> 01:47.654
plant. Product is stockpiled at the plant and sometimes

01:47.654 --> 01:50.554
underground. In the old mine there's also a Liwell

01:50.554 --> 01:53.367
plant, a small screen plant that works like a wash

01:53.367 --> 01:56.004
plant without water, making a clean product for

01:56.004 --> 01:58.691
asphalt mix at the asphalt plant nearby.

01:59.832 --> 02:02.020
Here are the focus hazards for this site.

02:02.020 --> 02:04.745
Roof and rib conditions in both the old and new

02:04.745 --> 02:08.195
mines. Knowing which mine, and which mine ID,

02:08.195 --> 02:11.445
you're working in. Surface drilling and blasting,

02:11.445 --> 02:14.370
so respect blast clearances and signals:

02:14.370 --> 02:17.395
a siren and strobe beacons, with entrances to the

02:17.395 --> 02:20.833
underground headers blocked. Mobile equipment underground

02:20.833 --> 02:23.407
and on the shared surface. The primary crusher

02:23.407 --> 02:25.870
in the pit and the conveyors up the hill.

02:25.870 --> 02:28.270
The secondary plant and stockpiles.

02:28.270 --> 02:31.670
The Liwell plant in the old mine. And silica dust,

02:31.670 --> 02:34.495
noise and diesel equipment. Stay clear of haul

02:34.495 --> 02:37.470
routes, the pit edge and crusher restricted areas

02:37.470 --> 02:39.532
unless you're authorized to be there.

02:40.662 --> 02:43.600
Up on the drill bench, access is bermed,

02:43.600 --> 02:45.825
and only the driller and the powder crew go up

02:45.825 --> 02:48.600
there. The highwall is marked with paint six feet

02:48.600 --> 02:51.825
back from the edge, and no one crosses that line.

02:51.825 --> 02:53.925
If weather apps show lightning during shooting

02:53.925 --> 02:56.700
time, the blaster in charge makes the call.

02:56.700 --> 02:59.825
The blast area is cleared, the entrance is guarded,

02:59.825 --> 03:02.537
and there's a fifteen-minute wait after strikes.

03:03.648 --> 03:07.048
You'll also see Clover Bottom's explosives magazines:

03:07.048 --> 03:10.448
steel boxes standing well apart in a big open area

03:10.448 --> 03:14.323
underground. Explosives are stored only in magazines.

03:14.323 --> 03:17.236
Stay away unless you're assigned to handle explosives,

03:17.236 --> 03:20.923
and never smoke or bring an open flame within 50 feet.

03:24.263 --> 03:26.912
The site supervisor is Andrew Burton,

03:26.912 --> 03:29.475
and the mine foreman is Braden Walters.

03:29.475 --> 03:31.925
Both came up running equipment at Boonesboro.

03:31.925 --> 03:35.388
Above them, Hunter Kenney is over all of our sites.

03:35.388 --> 03:37.275
Your instructor will introduce them.

03:37.275 --> 03:39.912
Miners check in and out on the tag board,

03:39.912 --> 03:41.975
and visitors have a separate check-in.

03:41.975 --> 03:44.550
There's one tag board: in-mine number one on the

03:44.550 --> 03:47.338
left, out in the middle, and in-mine number two

03:47.338 --> 03:49.875
on the right. Tag in under the mine you're actually

03:49.875 --> 03:52.575
entering. The tag-board trailer is also signed

03:52.575 --> 03:55.500
Emergency Assembly Area 1, one of the gathering

03:55.500 --> 03:59.688
points. From 2021 through mid-October 2026,

03:59.688 --> 04:02.713
inspectors cited the check-in and check-out standard

04:02.713 --> 04:06.438
three times here. When two mines share one surface,

04:06.438 --> 04:08.838
getting this right is how everyone gets accounted

04:08.838 --> 04:09.613
for.

04:10.732 --> 04:13.695
On site the speed limit is 15 miles an hour.

04:13.695 --> 04:16.120
Haul trucks have the right of way, and all roads

04:16.120 --> 04:19.382
are two-way, right-hand traffic. Radio before you

04:19.382 --> 04:22.095
approach a haul truck. Drivers being loaded stay

04:22.095 --> 04:25.432
in the cab. Before the shift, every operator completes

04:25.432 --> 04:28.282
the Quarry Equipment Pre-Operational Inspection

04:28.282 --> 04:31.320
and turns it in at the scale house or on the app.

04:31.320 --> 04:34.107
Equipment defects not corrected in a timely manner

04:34.107 --> 04:36.820
are the standard cited most at Clover Bottom,

04:36.820 --> 04:40.170
nine times across both mines. Your pre-shift check

04:40.170 --> 04:42.707
is where that starts. There are overhead power

04:42.707 --> 04:45.320
lines on the surface and at Mine number one,

04:45.320 --> 04:47.557
so no dumping or parking near them,

04:47.557 --> 04:49.795
no raised beds and no tarping.

04:50.951 --> 04:53.551
Pull cords or emergency stops are on the Liwell

04:53.551 --> 04:57.163
plant, the primary, the secondary, the pug mill,

04:57.163 --> 04:59.601
the surge tunnel and the recycle bin.

04:59.601 --> 05:02.089
Hearing protection is required around the plant

05:02.089 --> 05:04.801
while it's running and around the mine fans.

05:04.801 --> 05:07.001
Eyewash bottles are at the scale house and the

05:07.001 --> 05:10.351
breakroom, and the SDS binder is in the breakroom.

05:10.351 --> 05:13.626
Underground, stench gas goes into the intake fan,

05:13.626 --> 05:16.064
with radio and strobe warnings too.

05:16.064 --> 05:19.426
On the surface, the fire warning is a radio call.

05:19.426 --> 05:22.014
Escapeways are marked on the mine maps with green

05:22.014 --> 05:25.639
arrows. Underground, the primary escapeway is marked

05:25.639 --> 05:28.413
with white reflectors on the ribs, and the secondary

05:28.413 --> 05:31.413
with blue reflectors, along with reflective signs

05:31.413 --> 05:34.614
and arrows. For mine number one, maps are posted

05:34.614 --> 05:37.214
in the breakroom and at the drill steel building

05:37.214 --> 05:40.001
near the Liwell plant. For mine number two,

05:40.001 --> 05:42.201
they're in the breakroom and at the portal.

05:42.201 --> 05:44.201
The gathering points are the tag board,

05:44.201 --> 05:46.589
the old mine entrance, and behind the mine where

05:46.589 --> 05:49.101
the haul road to the asphalt plant is.

05:49.101 --> 05:51.163
Your instructor will walk you through the actual

05:51.163 --> 05:54.139
routes in each mine. Mine rescue for all of our

05:54.139 --> 05:56.451
sites comes from the Kentucky Division of Mine

05:56.451 --> 05:59.951
Safety's Crestwood and Hazard mine rescue stations.

06:03.285 --> 06:07.185
Since Allen took over the old mine in mid-2004,

06:07.185 --> 06:11.147
MSHA records 23 reportable worker injuries there.

06:11.147 --> 06:13.485
The new mine has none on record since it opened

06:13.485 --> 06:16.897
in 2021. The most serious pattern is ground falls

06:16.897 --> 06:21.522
at the face. Four times, in 2005, 2008,

06:21.522 --> 06:25.947
2011 and 2014, rock fell from the face or back

06:25.947 --> 06:28.572
onto miners who were hand-scaling, measuring a

06:28.572 --> 06:31.560
freshly scaled room, checking for loose rock or

06:31.560 --> 06:35.497
preparing to load a shot. In 2014, the rock above

06:35.497 --> 06:38.322
the one being pulled came down. Rock above can

06:38.322 --> 06:41.685
let go when rock below it moves. Scale only when

06:41.685 --> 06:44.847
trained and authorized, from a protected position,

06:44.847 --> 06:47.810
and re-examine after scaling and before loading.

06:48.938 --> 06:50.976
The other cases are worth knowing too.

06:50.976 --> 06:54.251
In 2021, a driller reached in to move a rock off

06:54.251 --> 06:56.913
a hose by the rib, and the rock shifted.

06:56.913 --> 06:59.476
Don't free equipment by hand next to a rib.

06:59.476 --> 07:04.050
In 2014 and 2017, drivers were hurt barring out

07:04.050 --> 07:07.626
plugged bins. Lock out, use approved tools and

07:07.626 --> 07:11.113
never work beneath the material. In 2018,

07:11.113 --> 07:13.876
one worker stepped into a catwalk hole left after

07:13.876 --> 07:16.563
a gearbox was removed, and another climbed over

07:16.563 --> 07:19.751
a conveyor. Barricade openings and never climb

07:19.751 --> 07:23.313
over conveyors. And in 2026, a piece of a track

07:23.313 --> 07:26.476
pin broke off and struck a contract mechanic.

07:26.476 --> 07:28.588
Use the right tools and keep others out of the

07:28.588 --> 07:29.763
line of fire.

07:30.884 --> 07:34.309
Inspectors issued 39 citations at the old mine

07:34.309 --> 07:37.747
and 11 at the new mine from 2021 through mid-October

07:37.747 --> 07:41.184
2026, most often for equipment defects,

07:41.184 --> 07:44.559
check-in records, parking, firefighting equipment,

07:44.559 --> 07:47.384
barricades and warning signs, and horns and backup

07:47.384 --> 07:50.322
alarms. So the takeaway for Clover Bottom:

07:50.322 --> 07:53.184
know which mine you're in, tag in at that mine,

07:53.184 --> 07:56.434
respect the face, and re-examine before you load.

07:57.579 --> 08:00.316
Before your first shift underground at Clover Bottom,

08:00.316 --> 08:02.454
make sure you can answer four questions.

08:02.454 --> 08:04.791
Which mine am I in today, number one or number

08:04.791 --> 08:07.816
two? What are my primary and secondary escapeways

08:07.816 --> 08:10.304
in that mine? Where is my gathering point on the

08:10.304 --> 08:13.066
shared surface? And who do I report to,

08:13.066 --> 08:15.354
and how do I reach them? If you can't answer all

08:15.354 --> 08:18.016
four, ask before you go in. And if you're ever

08:18.016 --> 08:20.629
near a pond, sump or pump where you could fall

08:20.629 --> 08:23.454
into water, a life jacket is required.

08:24.584 --> 08:27.747
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

08:27.747 --> 08:29.247
override this video.
